      "created_at": "2018-04-16T09:26:03Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-04-21T08:39:41Z",
      "body": "With the coming law regarding data collection ([GDPR/RGPD](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Data_Protection_Regulation)), I've to admit that YOURLS is not compliant at all out the box. IP collection, location gathering, etc. which are, merged with timestamp data, personally identifiable information.\r\n\r\nI remember me suggesting to move location resolution in a plugin (#1585), this is a new ***strong*** argument.\r\nRegarding IP, this is more complicated, but yes, it should be dropped or moved to anonymized fingerprints.",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
