      "created_at": "2018-04-25T18:34:08Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-04-25T18:34:08Z",
      "body": "@ozh https://github.com/sas101/yourls-pseudonymize is good but it\r\ndoesn't do enough. It would need to drop more ipv6 and ipv4 data, reduce\r\ntime resolution, get rid of user agent.  But I guess I was wrong about\r\nwhat is possible with a plugin. Also, the YOURLS plugin list has 0\r\nplugins, and google searches didn't lead me to that plugin. So, I didn't\r\nknow about that plugin at all.\r\n\r\nRight now for GPDR, my best guess is to turn on the option to not store\r\nanything in yourls_log, archive the YOURLS html pages that show\r\naggregate analysis, then wipe out yourls_log. Then I will look and wait\r\nfor a url shortener which can do more analysis while only storing\r\naggregate data and not personally identifiable data. It's not something\r\nI have the time to implement myself.\r\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
