      "created_at": "2018-05-28T08:58:08Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-05-28T08:58:08Z",
      "body": "Which IP is stored where? Adding a new short URL stores my (admin) IP address, yes. But I don't see where IP addresses by using (old or new) short ULRs are stored. Could you please elaborate?\r\n\r\nWhile typing I've got an idea what you could mean. If you let users add short URLs then their IPs would be logged in the table 'yourls_url'. Therefore, you have to hook additionally to the action \"insert_link\" (https://github.com/YOURLS/YOURLS/blob/master/includes/functions.php#L163) an remove the storing of the IP address.\r\n\r\nSince I am not letting any users add links I don't need to do this. But for the sake of completeness it should be added to the plug-in, when storing country codes.",
